1
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,820
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,760
Hahahahahaha!

3
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

4
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,560
I don't have one either, but don't worry.

5
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:11,960
Burning... Akaneru too.

6
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

8
00:01:23,770 --> 00:01:27,440
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

9
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,680
Awaken! Serious human, Ryokaku!

10
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:47,700
Backbone!

11
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,800
What's wrong, Chief Ohara?

12
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,240
Nothing's right. Just look at this.

13
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:01,480
These are the mock test scores from the sergeant
promotion exam the senior officer took the other day, right?

14
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,300
This is...

15
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,380
Too awful.

16
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:09,900
Retake. General knowledge exam retake.
Police practice retake.

17
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:12,700
I hear it's the lowest
score since the exam began.

18
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:14,520
I'm the one who's been humiliated!

19
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:17,120
Didn't you force her
to take the exam, Chief?

20
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,260
I didn't want to take it.

21
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:22,060
At your age,
you should take it at least once.

22
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:25,140
But someone this bad is
below elementary school level.

23
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:28,800
No matter what, if it were an elementary school problem,
I'd understand it.

24
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,720
Then who's the current prime minister?

25
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:35,220
No, no, no. Isn't it Ichiro Yamada?

26
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:37,920
That's wrong.

27
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,560
She might really be below
elementary school level.

28
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,580
Start over from elementary school.

29
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:48,300
Are you really going to make her do
elementary school-level questions?

30
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:52,720
It's so she gains enough knowledge and
education to not be embarrassed as a person.

31
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,060
Don't slack off.

32
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,560
Fine, I'll do it. Happy now?

33
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:58,760
Let's see...

34
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:25,020
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

35
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:29,300
So if you carelessly doze off, a pencil
gets stabbed right into your forehead.

36
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,840
A pencil in the forehead...

37
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,580
But now that I'm awake, I'll keep studying.

38
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,840
When I was young,
I fought off drowsiness like this

39
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:44,740
and threw myself into exam study.

40
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,520
Don't fall asleep this time.

41
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,460
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

42
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,580
With something this
dangerous right in front of me,

43
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,660
there's no way I could doze off,
even if I tried.

44
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,160
Drowsiness again...

45
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,260
If I fall asleep here...

46
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,660
A pencil in the forehead...

47
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:11,760
Falling asleep in that state, no less.

48
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,460
That guy is unbelievable.

49
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:14,960
But Ryo-san,

50
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,300
when it comes to games or model kits,

51
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,140
he goes for days without
sleep and doesn't mind a bit.

52
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:21,120
So why is it that
whenever he tries to study,

53
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,060
he drops off right away?

54
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,560
If I knew that,
would I be going through this hardship?

55
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:29,640
People generally put their full effort
into whatever they're interested in,

56
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:34,100
but Ryo-chan must be wired
differently from everyone else.

57
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,240
No way.

58
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,380
Exactly, that's how it is.

59
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,140
W-who's there?

60
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:41,360
Hey, Gorilla-kun,
it's over here, right here!

61
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:46,540
You, the eyeball...

62
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:46,960
No.

63
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,260
It's me, Gorilla-kun.

64
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:56,980
Actually, I've been really into
researching the human brain lately.

65
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,720
So why eyeballs...

66
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,280
Tiny

67
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:02,480
This was made to resemble a tuna eyeball.

68
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:08,320
Tuna eyeballs are packed with brain-boosting DHA,
you know.

69
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,080
Just call me Eyeball Santa.

70
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,980
You're way too suspicious!

71
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:19,280
The other day,
I snuck into Gorilla-kun's room

72
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:21,840
and secretly measured his brainwaves.

73
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,860
So that's what you were up to.

74
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:29,340
No wonder I've been having
nothing but weird dreams lately.

75
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,680
And the results revealed
something truly fascinating.

76
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:35,140
You see, this Gorilla-kun

77
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:37,900
isn't using his left brain at all.

78
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:39,500
What?

79
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:40,900
His left brain?

80
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,680
You're saying it isn't working?

81
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:43,500
Well, that's

82
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:45,580
the left brain.

83
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,240
The left side of the brain, you know.

84
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,380
I know that much.

85
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:52,740
The human brain is divided into
the right brain and the left brain.

86
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:56,900
The right brain governs
sensibilities like art and inspiration,

87
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:01,220
while the left brain governs reason,
like calculation and language processing.

88
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:04,700
That means his left
brain isn't working at all.

89
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:10,120
In other words, with no reason at work,
of course he's hopeless at tests.

90
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:13,700
But his sensibilities
are running at full power,

91
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:18,340
so he just follows his
instincts and keeps piling up debt

92
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,820
Don't be convinced.

93
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,600
But rest assured.

94
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,240
Pon pon pon pon

95
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,160
Gorilla-kun

96
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,400
What's that supposed to be?

97
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,440
It's a machine to wake up your brain.

98
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:36,560
With this,
your brain will start working too.

99
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,640
Really?

100
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,760
We've already finished the animal testing.

101
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,120
Take a look at this.

102
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:45,100
It's Nezumi Otokomae-kun.

103
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:46,740
Nezumi Otoko.

104
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,690
Nezumi Otokomae.

105
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:52,000
I named him that because
he's pretty handsome.

106
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:52,900
I see.

107
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,540
Thanks to Sano-kun,
he has awakened to intelligence.

108
00:06:56,900 --> 00:07:00,140
Nezumi Otokomae-kun, how do you say
"kiss" in Japanese?

109
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,400
Chuuun.

110
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,980
See that? That's intelligence.

111
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,720
Isn't that a grade-schooler's riddle?

112
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:09,280
Seems pretty suspicious, though.

113
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:13,220
Better than nothing. Let's give it a try.

114
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:19,940
Ready? Here we go. Sano-kun, switch!

115
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:20,360
Me.

116
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:31,580
How's it looking, big guy?
Let's see the brain activity display.

117
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:37,640
Really, no activity at all.
It seems he's in a very deep sleep.

118
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,540
Let's turn the output up a little.

119
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:47,420
There doesn't seem to be any change, though.

120
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:51,220
A normal person's activation
should have kicked in long ago.

121
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,080
Boost the output even more.

122
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,420
It still seems to be asleep.

123
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,360
Isn't it broken?

124
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:01,280
Ryo-chan's activation...

125
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,160
It's the other machine.

126
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,620
That can't be.

127
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,620
My invention is perfect.

128
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,020
Power up!

129
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,440
My head's starting to tingle!

130
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:13,960
This machine!

131
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:16,840
Your activation won't wake
up with just a little effort.

132
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,120
I've been patient, damn it!

133
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:23,320
Still not waking up?! You're a stubborn one!

134
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,960
Wake up! Wake up!

135
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,100
Professor!

136
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,860
Isn't this getting too dangerous?

137
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,000
Not yet!

138
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:32,780
Activate! Wake up!

139
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,060
Ryotsu, are you all right?

140
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,300
S-Senpai.

141
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:04,820
Ryo-chan is studying.

142
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:08,500
Ryotsu, you...

143
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:11,040
I'm in the middle of solving
this problem right now.

144
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,400
Please be quiet.

145
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,080
Done!

146
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,060
What is it, Chief?

147
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:22,380
Ryotsu, you really are Ryotsu, aren't you?

148
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:26,740
Did the shock of that explosion switch
his personality with someone else again?

149
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,720
Don't be ridiculous.

150
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,000
I'm still me.

151
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,560
But suddenly studying like this...

152
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:36,840
I don't understand it myself,
but the moment the explosion happened,

153
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:41,780
I suddenly felt like I
could solve the problems.

154
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:46,840
So I just tried them, and I'm solving
them easily, almost like it's fun.

155
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:52,080
Why did I struggle with such simple problems until now?
It's strange.

156
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:53,840
All of them are correct.

157
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:56,620
S-so, Ryotsu's intelligence is...

158
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,420
Gorilla!

159
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:01,160
Gorilla-kun's intelligence
has fully awakened!

160
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:05,620
At this rate, the day Gorilla-kun
evolves into a human is near!

161
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:07,980
He was human from the start!

162
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,060
Here's some tea. Take a little break.

163
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:18,040
Once you finish this problem, you've
been keeping at it every day, haven't you?

164
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:21,040
Ever since then, he's been studying
whenever he has a spare moment.

165
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:24,740
The drill book Chief Ohara bought
him at first was finished long ago,

166
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,880
and now he's even buying
his own problem books.

167
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,440
What a change

168
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,020
What's all this studying for?
Are you planning to get into university?

169
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,640
I'm thinking of taking
the sergeant promotion exam.

170
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,680
Did Ryotsu really say that?

171
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,780
That's quite a funny joke.

172
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:50,420
Didn't he get the lowest score
ever on the mock exam the other day?

173
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:53,740
That idiot,
is he going to embarrass me again?

174
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:56,900
But Ryo-chan has been
studying lately, though.

175
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,660
The exam is next month.

176
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:02,540
Just the other day he was doing elementary school problems.
There's no way he'll make it in time.

177
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:06,080
Today he was doing last year's University
of Tokyo entrance exam questions.

178
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,380
He got nearly every question right.

179
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:09,680
What?

180
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:15,360
It seems the power of his left brain, which has
been asleep for decades, has suddenly been unleashed.

181
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:20,120
At this rate, he might pass the
sergeant promotion exam on the first try.

182
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:23,680
No, he could even go straight
for the inspector promotion exam.

183
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,620
That Ryotsu?

184
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:32,540
But the sergeant promotion exam isn't just a written test.
It also has interviews and police practical skills.

185
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:34,600
Can he really handle that?

186
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:36,500
What about that part too?

187
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,120
Maybe he'll manage somehow.

188
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,120
He should be arriving any time now.

189
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:46,940
Duty doesn't start for
another thirty minutes.

190
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,920
He's been early every day lately.

191
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,700
That chronically late Kankichi?

192
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,160
Good morning, Chief Ohara.

193
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:55,380
Good morning.

194
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,220
What a beautiful day it is today.

195
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,960
Is that really Ryotsu?

196
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,820
Then who else would it be?

197
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,460
He's dressed differently than usual.

198
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,720
He's just wearing his uniform
the way it's meant to be worn.

199
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,160
It's just that until
now he was far too sloppy.

200
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,540
S-so that's it.

201
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:18,520
Excuse me,
I'd like to ask you for directions.

202
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,300
Yes, right away.

203
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,380
For that, if you go straight down this road,

204
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,200
there's a tobacco shop on your right.

205
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,660
Turn right there,

206
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:29,500
Ryotsu has been working seriously,

207
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,640
and we're really being helped.

208
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:34,040
He studies for his entrance
exams whenever he has free time.

209
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:37,560
Now he's become a model police officer,
hasn't he?

210
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,360
I can't believe it.

211
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,700
Well then.

212
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:46,380
Ryotsu,
I hear you've been studying hard lately.

213
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:49,100
I just hadn't been
studying at all until now.

214
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:53,420
By the way, do you know Article
31 of the Constitution of Japan?

215
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:56,920
No one shall be

216
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,360
deprived of life or liberty,

217
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,120
nor be subjected to criminal penalties,

218
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:04,580
That's correct, Chief.

219
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:08,380
Then the regulations on police questioning

220
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:12,580
when, judging reasonably from unusual
behavior and other circumstances,

221
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:18,740
there are sufficient grounds to suspect someone of
having committed or being about to commit some crime,

222
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:28,100
or who is deemed to know about a crime already committed or one about to be committed,
may be questioned.

223
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,460
He's really rattling off the answers,
isn't he?

224
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:33,760
His brain is working at full speed.

225
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:40,040
Oh no, at this rate Ryotsu will really
make sergeant in this promotion exam.

226
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:42,240
And then he'll be an inspector right away.

227
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:46,000
He won't end up becoming a superintendent or even a chief superintendent,
will he?

228
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:48,340
If that happens...

229
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:51,420
Akimoto-kun, could you bring me some tea?

230
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,760
Yes, right away.

231
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:56,880
Akimoto-kun,
please fax these documents to headquarters.

232
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,200
Yes

233
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,560
What's wrong, Akimoto-kun?

234
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:04,600
I don't really understand
how to use the machine.

235
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:08,940
You idiot! That's exactly why
you're a perennial sergeant!

236
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,380
Use Sano more! Sano!

237
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,980
I'm terribly sorry.

238
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:18,360
We must avoid that at all costs.

239
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,960
So it's just you, Ryotsu?

240
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,760
Where are the others?

241
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,480
Reiko went to the bookstore.

242
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,140
I see.

243
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:39,660
I actually got hold of some good sake.

244
00:14:39,660 --> 00:14:40,740
How about a cup?

245
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,600
That sounds good.

246
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:46,380
If I drink in the daytime,
my performance evaluation will drop,

247
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,900
and I'll lose all motivation to study.

248
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:51,000
If I keep this up every day,
I'm sure to fail the exam.

249
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:51,520
Chief.

250
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,820
I'll have some after work hours.

251
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,500
If you keep talking so leisurely,

252
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,720
the others will notice too!

253
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,140
You won't be able to hog it all!

254
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:05,860
Sake is meant to be enjoyed together,
isn't it?

255
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,900
Ryotsu

256
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,300
you

257
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:15,260
What a narrow-minded man I've been!

258
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:18,660
To think I was trying to get
in the way of such a fine man!

259
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,180
I'd like to crawl into a hole.

260
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,200
Ryotsu

261
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,580
Be sure to pass the exam this time.

262
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,440
Is there anything I can do to help?

263
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,900
Just tell me whatever you need.

264
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,700
What's with you all of a sudden?

265
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,560
I'm back.

266
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,300
Chief Ohara

267
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,420
What's wrong?

268
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:38,300
You two,
please help Ryotsu pass the exam too.

269
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,280
That sound...

270
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,220
Long time no see.

271
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,340
You there,
officers of the Kōen-mae police box.

272
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:50,600
You...

273
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:51,920
Who was it again?

274
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,840
If you've forgotten, let me remind you.

275
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:58,740
I'm the super-rich Renji Shiratori!

276
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:00,800
Now I remember.

277
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:05,200
Reiko, I've reserved the
finest restaurant in Akasaka.

278
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,660
Let's enjoy ourselves
to the fullest tonight.

279
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,640
Didn't Shiratori Heavy
Industries go bankrupt?

280
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:15,240
They say the phoenix rises
again and again from the trees.

281
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:19,520
Shiratori Heavy Industries
rose again like a phoenix, too.

282
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,740
Come on, let's go, Reiko.

283
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,700
Hold on, Mr. Shiratori!

284
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,460
Something's missing.

285
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:31,140
Money! Money! Money!

286
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:36,980
Right, normally the super-poor Ryotsu
Kankichi Knight should pop out right about now.

287
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:38,820
Isn't he here?

288
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:44,780
He's here after all.

289
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:47,740
See? Ryotsu's studying. Don't disturb him.

290
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:51,720
Studying?
Save the jokes until you've seen this.

291
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:52,720
This.

292
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:55,760
Stop it!

293
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,320
This time it's not kids' play money!

294
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:02,700
It's real money!

295
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:10,060
Don't tell me you're unfazed seeing this much cash!
Don't ignore it!

296
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:17,520
Hey, there's a rule for this! If you pick it up,
you get a finder's reward. Even kids know that!

297
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:29,260
You only get the reward for lost property. If someone drops it right in front of you, it doesn't count.
That's right. By the way, when you report lost property, the reward ranges from 5 to 20 percent.

298
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:32,200
It doesn't have to be ten percent, though.

299
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,900
Of course I knew that.

300
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:38,880
I just wanted to test
your knowledge a little.

301
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:42,480
And as for those who clearly
gave up their ownership,

302
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,960
it goes to whoever picks it up first.

303
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,120
Like money you scattered yourself,
for example.

304
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,900
This money is mine!

305
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,440
Nobody touch it!

306
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:54,080
What?

307
00:17:56,260 --> 00:17:57,060
No.

308
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:00,540
How dare you embarrass me
in front of Reiko like that!

309
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:02,040
You just wait.

310
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,520
He's gone.

311
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:11,620
Still, to keep studying with that
much cash right in front of him.

312
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:14,720
He's nothing like the
Ryo-chan we used to know.

313
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:17,640
I'll explain that.

314
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:21,560
Professor Esaki.

315
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,240
Wh-what is that getup?

316
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:24,520
A nurikabe?

317
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,660
Looks just like a sweet potato,
any way you look at it.

318
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:28,480
Right?

319
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:30,500
So, Professor...?

320
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,200
Why are you dressed like that?

321
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:36,440
The energy that drives
the human brain is sugar.

322
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:39,460
When it comes to foods high in sugar,
sweet potatoes come to mind.

323
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,300
For that reason alone.

324
00:18:41,860 --> 00:18:47,040
Now, about this gorilla, in the human
head there's actually instinct and reason,

325
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:50,560
meaning the right brain and left
brain are constantly fighting.

326
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,020
Normally,
they take turns winning and losing.

327
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:58,800
My left brain has been asleep for decades,
so it has an excess of power.

328
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:05,020
That's why I've completely suppressed my right
brain and become a super-rational human being.

329
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:07,420
Excellent, excellent.

330
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:10,360
But somehow, it doesn't seem like Ryo-chan.

331
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:13,920
Well then, I'm off to the exam.

332
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,060
Good luck out there.

333
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:16,940
Yes.

334
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:20,620
Now that my left brain is working,
I finally understand.

335
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:24,760
how right the Chief was in
all the warnings he gave me.

336
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:28,560
And how much the Chief worried about me.

337
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:29,900
Ryotsu...

338
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:31,580
Go far.

339
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:34,640
Become a far better police
officer than I ever was.

340
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:34,840
Chief.

341
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,060
Ryotsu!

342
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:37,440
Ryotsu!

343
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:45,040
Ryo-chan, if you get promoted,
you'll be leaving this police box, right?

344
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:47,340
Probably so.

345
00:19:47,340 --> 00:19:51,060
Once Ryo-san is gone, this place will
just become an ordinary police box.

346
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:53,600
He's going to grow from here.

347
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,880
Let's send him off with a smile.

348
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:57,440
Yes, we should.

349
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:02,140
I've been waiting for you,
you poor common man.

350
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:07,600
Shiratori, you...

351
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:10,380
I know what you're going to say.

352
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,460
Aren't you cold dressed like that?

353
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:15,860
But I'm not cold at all.

354
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:27,480
I've got this bag of ten-thousand-yen bills,
you know.

355
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:28,420
That.

356
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,600
It feels great.

357
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:36,740
This contains all of Shinatori
Heavy Industries' assets.

358
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:40,740
Keeping it could count as
embezzling lost property, though.

359
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,360
I'll let it slide for now.

360
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:44,600
My exam's coming up, after all.

361
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:45,740
Don't ignore me!

362
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:48,340
How about that

363
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:53,980
Your favorite bills! Get down on
your hands and knees and pick them up!

364
00:20:54,480 --> 00:21:01,600
I won't fall for your provocation. I'm in a hurry, so excuse me.
Look, look, there's more! You really want it, don't you?

365
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:06,780
I could give you some, you know. Money's great.
It makes even your heart feel rich.

366
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:10,820
There are plenty of things in this
world more important than money.

367
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:15,180
What's wrong? My legs... my legs won't move!

368
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:19,220
Since we've got the chance,
let's just take it.

369
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:22,080
We've always done it this way up till now,
haven't we?

370
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:26,560
No way. You've failed time and again because money lured you in,
remember?

371
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:29,700
Are you telling me to just let these
bills right in front of us slip by?

372
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:32,900
That's right.
You can't give in to that kind of greed.

373
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:36,800
Grr, you've got a lot of nerve, going on like
that while I've been keeping quiet and listening!

374
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,500
I don't want your money, you know!

375
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,160
Don't joke around!

376
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:45,780
W-wait!
Let's talk this over calmly and rationally.

377
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:50,320
I hate you! I'm going to do this to you!

378
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:51,040
Yaaah!

379
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:54,780
You don't need to show your
face for another hundred years!

380
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,740
Hahahaha!

381
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:59,380
H-hey, p-pauper!

382
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:06,560
Hehehe! Money makes the world go round!

383
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:07,440
Heh!

384
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:09,180
Money, money, money, money!

385
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:12,340
Stop! That's my dad's
company's entire fortune!

386
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:14,500
You said I could have it earlier!

387
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,120
My legs, they're, they're coming off...
they're...

388
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:19,780
I'm carrying it to my room!

389
00:22:20,780 --> 00:22:21,920
Please, just that far first.

390
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:22,880
Y-yes.

391
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:27,600
Hey, gorilla!

392
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:29,620
Don't you want some bills?

393
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:31,320
It's cash, you know.

394
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:32,920
Of course, I'll take it.

395
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,140
I said so.

396
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,480
Bechikaru

397
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:40,160
The cash

398
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:42,380
Hey, where's the cash?

399
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:43,840
It's right here, isn't it?

400
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:47,060
The cash,
packed with sugar to fuel the brain,

401
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:49,520
will guarantee I pass the exam.

402
00:22:50,780 --> 00:22:51,560
Cash

403
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,760
Real cash...

404
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,280
Water, water, water!

405
00:22:59,280 --> 00:22:59,940
Yes.

406
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:07,820
There's water over there!

407
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,860
Water! Water!

408
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,400
This is

409
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:15,600
a gas station!

410
00:23:22,260 --> 00:23:23,300
This is mine.

411
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:26,860
Miss Reiko brought this just for me.

412
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:27,580
This is...

413
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:33,080
I hear Ryo-chan's Sanon has
fallen into a deep sleep again.

414
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,700
So his promotion to sergeant

415
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,640
is out of the question for now, then.

416
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:42,380
But this suits Ryo-chan better,
don't you think?

417
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:44,040
As for Shiratori-san,

418
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:47,360
they say the phoenix rises
from the flames again and again.

419
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:51,860
But if all his money burns to ashes,

420
00:23:51,860 --> 00:23:54,240
it'll take a long time to revive.

421
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:58,960
Come on, be more rational.

422
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:02,380
This is the way I live.

423
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:20,380
Like someone is calling out to me,
on an afternoon after the rain

424
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:27,100
Walking while looking back,
my hand pulled by the gacha

425
00:24:27,100 --> 00:24:34,220
That strange feeling I had back then

426
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:39,500
So on the arcade's tiles,

427
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones

428
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:51,460
Everyone was a child once,

429
00:24:51,460 --> 00:24:53,600
but everyone forgets

430
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,580
politicians with their self-important faces,

431
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,900
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too

432
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:03,860
Go on, turn the corner

433
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:06,460
that corner

434
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:11,680
You can meet everyone, everyone

435
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:16,300
Over there, there's Kame-ari

436
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:19,600
I'm sure there's Kame-ari

437
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:24,920
Come on, everyone, to our town!

438
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,360
Thank you.

439
00:25:30,460 --> 00:25:33,860
An investigation drill using
the PHS reverse-tracing system.

440
00:25:33,860 --> 00:25:36,940
As the culprit who escapes to the very end,
Tora Keep,

441
00:25:36,940 --> 00:25:38,280
"Leave it to me," he said.

442
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:41,080
When it comes to running away,
this Ryotsu seems to be the one for it.

443
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:43,320
Nobody can beat him.

444
00:25:43,320 --> 00:25:47,320
Look forward to my dancing
investigation next time, too.

445
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,980
Here it is, Kame-ari!

446
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,500
Well, surely, Kame-ari!

447
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:59,340
Come on, everyone, to our town!

448
00:26:00,460 --> 00:26:00,940
Thank you.

